"\n    },\n    "markdown_overview": {\n      "description": "Comprehensive Markdown document (.md) explaining: (1) The core PyTorch/Deep Learning concept, (2) How it directly relates to the Phase 1 dataset telemetry & failure modes, and (3) What the student is trying to solve in the hands-on exercise.",\n      "title": "Markdown Overview",\n      "type": "string"\n    }\n  },\n  "required": [\n    "title",\n    "domain_context",\n    "problem_statement",\n    "learning_objectives",\n    "target_input_shape",\n    "target_output_shape",\n    "suggested_focus",\n    "markdown_overview"\n  ],\n  "title": "ProblemStatementSchema",\n  "type": "object"\n}\n\n            Make sure to return an instance of the JSON, not the schema itself\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nYou are an expert AI Curriculum Director and Applied Deep Learning Educator.\nFormulate a domain-grounded coding problem statement for module \'NumPy Basics & Data Structures\' (Week 1).\nDirectives: Explore dataset directory structure, NumPy array operations, and matrix normalization.\nDifficulty: Beginner\n\n--- PHASE 1 PIPELINE TELEMETRY ---\nDataset/Config: skin_cancer_testing_config.yaml\nTotal Rows Processed: 3297\nOverall Accuracy: 90.57% | AUC-ROC: 0.9709\nClass Balance: {\'benign\': 1800, \'malignant\': 1497}\nError Telemetry: {\'benign_predicted_as_malignant\': 146, \'malignant_predicted_as_benign\': 165}\nPer-Class Metrics: {\'benign\': {\'precision\': 0.9093, \'sensitivity_recall\': 0.9189, \'specificity\': 0.8898, \'false_negative_rate\': 0.0811, \'false_positive_rate\': 0.1102, \'f1_score\': 0.9141}, \'malignant\': {\'precision\': 0.9012, \'sensitivity_recall\': 0.8898, \'specificity\': 0.9189, \'false_negative_rate\': 0.1102, \'false_positive_rate\': 0.0811, \'f1_score\': 0.8955}}\nClass Labels: {\'0\': \'benign\', \'1\': \'malignant\'}\n5-Fold CV Mean Accuracy: 0.8811 | Mean F1: 0.8799\nPipeline Artifact Columns: [\'image_path\', \'ground_truth\', \'predicted_class\', \'probabilities\', \'segmented_image\', \'mask\']\n\n--- STATISTICAL CONTRASTIVE SAMPLES (AGENT 0 REFERENCE) ---\n[TOP_SUCCESS SAMPLE]: {\'image_path\': \'/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1539.jpg\', \'ground_truth\': \'benign\', \'predicted_class\': \'benign\', \'probabilities\': \'[0.9997135996818542, 0.0002863977279048413]\', \'segmented_image\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/segmented/1539_segmented_20260820_212936.png\', \'mask\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/masks/1539_mask_20260820_212936.png\'}\n[HARD_FAILURE SAMPLE]: {\'image_path\': \'/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1649.jpg\', \'ground_truth\': \'benign\', \'predicted_class\': \'malignant\', \'probabilities\': \'[0.06674916297197342, 0.9332507848739624]\', \'segmented_image\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/segmented/1649_segmented_20260820_212935.png\', \'mask\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/masks/1649_mask_20260820_212935.png\'}\n[BOUNDARY_UNCERTAINTY SAMPLE]: {\'image_path\': \'/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1303.jpg\', \'ground_truth\': \'benign\', \'predicted_class\': \'malignant\', \'probabilities\': \'[0.49796172976493835, 0.502038300037384]\', \'segmented_image\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/segmented/1303_segmented_20260820_212937.png\', \'mask\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/masks/1303_mask_20260820_212937.png\'}\n[MINORITY_SAMPLE SAMPLE]: {\'image_path\': \'/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1135.jpg\', \'ground_truth\': \'benign\', \'predicted_class\': \'benign\', \'probabilities\': \'[0.8938646912574768, 0.1061352789402008]\', \'segmented_image\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/segmented/1135_segmented_20260820_212924.png\', \'mask\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/masks/1135_mask_20260820_212924.png\'}\n\nFORMULATION DIRECTIVES:\n1. Analyze Phase 1 telemetry (error counts, class imbalance, precision/recall per class, and contrastive samples).\n2. Formulate a realistic, domain-specific problem statement using the exact target class names and dataset metrics provided in telemetry.\n3. Specify clear synthetic tensor input/output shape contracts matching the dataset modality.\n4. Focus the exercise on addressing the primary model failure modes and performance gaps discovered in Phase 1.\n5. Write a comprehensive `markdown_overview` document formatted in Github-flavored Markdown containing:\n   - `# [Module Title] Concept Overview`\n   - `## 1. Theoretical Background` (explaining the deep learning concept)\n   - `## 2. Domain & Pipeline Telemetry Grounding` (explaining how this concept connects to the Phase 1 dataset & error cases)\n   - `## 3. Hands-on Student Exercise & Objectives` (explaining what the student is building, implementing, and solving)\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=1.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=8192, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=GuidedDecodingParams(json=None, regex=None, choice=None, grammar=None, json_object=True, backend=None, whitespace_pattern=None)), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
